queries   : 2 accepted, 512-d, crc ok
            scored as z = (cos - background) / std, where the background is this room's
            own mean over its first 30 frames and is then FROZEN - so a thing left in
            shot keeps its score instead of decaying into the furniture. 'N' re-learns
            it, 'H' switches to tracking. The COCO figures below are only the seed for
            frame 0 and the fixed std.
            std is THIS ROOM's, measured over the same 30 frames ('S' switches to COCO's).
            The thresholds below still mean the 90th percentile of a background; the
            background they now mean it against is this room empty, not 5000 COCO photos.
            z is EMA-smoothed at 0.35 (~5 frames) before ranking, so a state has to
            persist for about two seconds to be called.
            an opened book       match above z 1.23   (COCO background -0.151 +- 0.030, so cos -0.114)
            a closed book        match above z 1.23   (COCO background -0.159 +- 0.035, so cos -0.116)

loop      : capture, 8 convs on the T8, pool and head, then one cosine per query. 'B' for BOOTSEL, 'R' to restart,
            'P' to dump the next frame for host/cam.py, 'V' to dump its 512 floats for host/caption.py,
            'E' to provoke a fault so D1 shows its fault display, 'H' to freeze/unfreeze the background,
            'S' to switch the spread between this room's and COCO's, 'W' to hang on purpose and see
            the watchdog name the stage, 'C' to stall the camera bus on purpose and see it cost one frame,
            'U' to drop off USB on purpose and watch it come back, 'I' to drop off and refuse to,
            'N' to forget it and learn it again from now. 'P' and 'V' together describe the same frame.
            'O' closes the timing window, prints it and flips the capture between overlapped and serial;
            'D' does the same and flips the trigger between late and at-the-collect, which is #14's A/B.
            scores are z against this room's background, ranked; '*' means over its threshold.
            '1'..'6' enrol the next 20 frames as that class. Two classes in and the board decides
            by nearest reference instead of by threshold, and calls a frame absent when it is
            further than 2.0 sep from every one of them - see M21. The empty scene is not
            enrolled and '0' does nothing; see #18.
            The first 30 frames set the baseline and it is then frozen, so anything left in
            shot KEEPS its score. Point the camera at the empty scene for those frames.
            Send a new set at any time to re-query - that resets the baseline too.

